  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(\\theta)=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & \\cos \\theta & -1 \\\\ -\\sin \\theta & 1 & -\\cos \\theta \\\\ -1 & \\sin \\theta & 1\\end{array}\\right|$. Suppose $A$ and $B$ are respectively maximum and minimum values of $f(\\theta)$. Then $(A, B)$ is equal to",
